## WHO WE ARE

**Boundry.AI** is a private, offline-first cybersecurity business run by Jason Morgan
and his partner Peta. All client data stays on-machine — zero cloud processing.
The AI backend is a local Ollama instance (llama3.1:8b on an AMD RX 7700 XT GPU).
Anthropic/Claude API is the fallback only.

**Jason** — technical lead. Builds everything in this repo.
**Peta** — business and marketing lead. Has a separate toolset (C:\Dev\peta-tools\).

**Target market:** SMBs, starting with the cannabis vertical (cannabis businesses can't
run Google/Meta ads, making AI search visibility and cybersecurity critical for them).

**Stage:** Pre-revenue. Building alongside day jobs. First clients coming soon.
The goal is a 2-person operation where the tools do 80% of the work.


## BUSINESS LINES

1. **Cybersecurity** — The Flask command center (this repo). Continuous monitoring,
   SIEM, incident response, AI-generated reports. Monthly retainer model.
2. **GEO/SAO** — Generative Engine Optimization (getting businesses into AI search
   answers). Peta's domain. Tools in C:\Dev\peta-tools\.


## THE MACHINE

- Windows 11, AMD RX 7700 XT (24GB VRAM), 24GB RAM, 2TB SSD
- Ollama v0.24.0 running llama3.1:8b on GPU (http://localhost:11434)
- Open WebUI at http://localhost:8080
- Flask app at http://localhost:5000
- SQLite for local dev (PostgreSQL via DATABASE_URL for production)


